        "label": "Temperature corrected energy usage for heating in dwellings, multi-dwelling and non-residential premises including the energy arised from heating pumps, 1995-, kWh/m2 by Measure and Year",
        "source": "Swedish Energy Agency",
        "updated": "2026-05-20T07:00:00Z",
        "note": [
          "Note. There is some uncertainty in the statistics and in the method for temperature correction of energy use for heating, as relatively warm (2014) and cold (2010) years give a different outcome. Official statistics on energy use in single-family homes, apartment buildings and premises only include the losses that occur in the building. The losses that occur in the production and distribution of electricity and district heating are not included. If a household switches from, for example, oil heating to district heating, the energy use in single-family homes, apartment buildings and premises in statistical reports decreases, while the energy use for district heating production increases. This is given that the building's heat demand is still the same.",
          "<A HREF='https://www.energimyndigheten.se/energisystem-och-analys/nulaget-i-energisystemet/energiindikatorer/' >More information about Energy indicators</A>",
